From 5a71f6b05dd953ed66240b109c7b9c19a50ab96a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 16:45:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Add a single pricing engine as the source of truth for
 all money

The app had four independent money calculations that disagreed with each
other. For function 1 of event 1 they produced three different answers:

  services page sidebar   $6,053.00 (charges only)
  event financials        $7,384.66 (22% gratuity, 0% tax)
  printed BEO             $7,868.90 (hard-coded 8% tax, 22% gratuity)

This adds calculateFunctionPricing / calculateEventPricing as the one place
money is computed. Design rules:

  * Rates are configuration, never constants. Sales and occupancy tax come
    from revenue_centers; service charge and gratuity from service_fees.
    An unconfigured rate yields zero AND a warning, rather than silently
    substituting an invented default -- a wrong number on a signed BEO is
    worse than a visibly missing one. The old code fell back to `0.22`
    whenever it could not find a fee whose *name* contained "22%".
  * Only items explicitly selected, with quantity > 0, are billable.
  * Adjustments pro-rate by share of charges rather than splitting evenly,
    which used to move money between revenue centers.
  * Taxable service fees widen the tax base.
  * Rounding happens once per revenue-center subtotal, never per line.

Pure helpers (isBillable, computeLineTotal, computeLineCost, round2) are
exported so they can be tested without a database.

