From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 16:45:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Route all money through the pricing engine, and honour
 item selection

Attaching a menu template billed the entire catalogue as if the client had
ordered every item on it. Function 1 has 77 items across 7 menus of which
exactly ONE is selected; the app charged the sum of all 77 ($6,053.00)
instead of the one selected item ($160.00) -- a 37x overbill. The
`selected` column already existed and was returned by the API; no consumer
ever filtered on it.

  * financials / functionFinancials now delegate to the pricing engine.
  * GET /functions/:id/menus overlays server-computed line, service-type and
    menu totals plus selected/total item counts, so the client never does
    money arithmetic.
  * Applying a menu template now copies `cost` from the catalog alongside
    price and revenue center -- without it every margin reads 100% -- and
    writes selected=false explicitly: a template makes items AVAILABLE, not
    ordered.
  * Copying a menu preserves selection, quantities and hourly-charge fields;
    previously duplicating a priced menu silently zeroed it.
  * POST /functions/:id/post captures a real financial snapshot instead of
    writing zeros, so the Event Lifecycle snapshot column works.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
