From 0ed6bb36c03bbb334f8a6a757e9a2c3cbc72b550 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 16:45:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Stop date-only values shifting a day across screens

Event 1 is stored as 2026-05-23 to 2026-05-25. The events list and the event
detail header rendered it as May 22-24, while the timeline, reports and BEO
rendered it correctly -- so the same event showed two different date ranges
depending on which screen you were on.

Cause: `new Date("2026-05-23")` parses as UTC midnight, and formatting that
in any timezone west of UTC yields the previous day. A few screens already
worked around it with `+ "T00:00:00"`; most did not.

Adds lib/date.ts, which parses date-only strings at LOCAL midnight, and
routes every calendar-date display through it. True timestamps (createdAt,
updatedAt) are left timezone-aware, as they should be.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Aar9a19BttoKXAyn5iy7Mk
