From 53ce17c6b7b5f984965f2e4b5b41846c294c4d61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 16:45:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Make the BEO and services builder read money from the
 server

The BEO hard-coded 8% sales tax, 22% gratuity and a 1.30 multiplier for the
grand total, and printed every item of every attached menu template. It now:

  * reads charges, service charge, gratuity and taxes from the pricing
    engine, so it cannot disagree with the financials pages;
  * lists only items the client actually selected, and omits menus with
    nothing ordered rather than printing empty sections;
  * shows the function's room -- Location/Room read `fn.location`, which
    does not exist; the API has always returned `locationName`. The same
    typo blanked the location on the function detail page and left the
    function switcher reading "in TBD".

The services sidebar gains a real breakdown (subtotal / service charge /
gratuity / tax / grand total) plus a banner surfacing unconfigured-rate
warnings. The menu editor no longer estimates tax and gratuity with its own
constants; it shows a selected-item count and defers to the authoritative
figures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Aar9a19BttoKXAyn5iy7Mk
